 "title": "Zinc Regulation in Cells and Organisms",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around zinc regulation in various cells and organisms. Zinc (Zn) is a crucial element that is bound to different complexes, such as Zn coordination complexes, and is involved in homeostasis. It is imported into cells through proteins like ZRT1, Cot1, and Zrc1. Zn is also present in different compartments, including cytosol, vacuoles, and mitochondria. The regulation of Zn is studied using methods like FTS and CYT10, which have peaks for different Zn complexes. FluoZin-3 is used to spike CYT, and Zn-GSH and Zn-citrate are present in various organisms, including E. coli and yeast cells.",
